# ui-panels.mdc

# UI panels — bold title required

**Panel refactors:** follow step-by-step priorities in [`docs/ui-panel-refactor.md`](../../docs/ui-panel-refactor.md). When the user names a priority (P1–P10), read that section, check off migration steps, and update the progress log.

**Every new or refactored editor panel** (left column, right column, nested sections) must use a **bold title row** from `ui/widgets/panel_header.py`. Do not use `QGroupBox("Title")`, plain `QLabel` panel titles, or the native `QGroupBox` title for the panel name.

## Title helpers

| Helper | When to use |
| ------ | ----------- |
| `create_titled_panel_layout(panel, title, trailing_widgets)` | Title + header buttons (Groups, Layers, Compass `×`, …) |
| `create_simple_titled_panel_layout(panel, title)` | Title only (Palettes, Materials, Selector, Structure, …) |
| `create_nested_group_layout(group, title)` | Nested `QGroupBox` sections (Selected Block, Site grid, Render types, …) |

All three call `add_panel_title_row`, which sets the title `QLabel` font to **bold**.

## Setup checklist for a new panel

1. Subclass `QGroupBox` (or wrap content in a `QGroupBox` inside a column).
2. `super().__init__(parent)` — **no** title string argument.
3. `layout = create_simple_titled_panel_layout(self, "Panel name")` (or `create_titled_panel_layout` if there are header buttons).
4. Add fields and controls to `layout` below the title row.
5. Wire signals in `ui/main_window.py`; document in `docs/ui.md`.

## Do not

- `QGroupBox("My panel")` for the outer or nested section title
- Duplicate title styling in per-panel stylesheets
- Skip the title row on “small” panels (palette, tool hints, settings blocks included)

## Icon buttons (when needed)

- Size: `panel_icon_size()` from `ui/toolbar_icons.py` (18×18).
- Factory: `make_panel_tool_button(icon, tooltip, clicked=...)` from `ui/widgets/panel_tool_button.py`.
- Dismissible panels: `make_panel_close_button` (`assets/ui/window-close.svg`) + `close_requested` signal; add a matching checkable **View** menu action in `ui/main_window.py`.
- Expose actions via **signals**; wire in `ui/main_window.py`.

## Examples

- `palette_panel.py` — `create_simple_titled_panel_layout(self, "Palettes")`
- `layer_list_panel.py` / `groups_panel.py` — `create_titled_panel_layout` + four actions
- `properties_panel.py` — nested `create_nested_group_layout` for Selected Block / Grid cell; inspector combo changes live-apply via `brush_inspector_changed` / `brush_blockstate_changed` → `MainWindow._apply_inspector_to_selected_cell` (Signature: `properties-inspector-live-apply`)
- `preview_toolbar.py` — compact `QWidget` row (not a `QGroupBox`); Previous/Next + trailing zoom label for Viewer preview (2D only)
- `orbit_preview_widget.py` — lazy-loaded `QOpenGLWidget` for 3D orbit; created on first **3D** toggle, not at `PreviewPanel` import; `QMatrix4x4.lookAt` uses `QVector3D` (Qt6 API). **Render class:** classify tokens with `orbit_render_class()` before editing orbit geometry — Signature: `orbit-render-class-routing`; glossary `docs/render-types.md` § Orbit render class. **Partial blocks:** stairs/slabs → opaque atlas tiles in `orbit_face_textures.py` (not 2D masks); fences/walls → masked bakes + `sample.a < 0.05` discard in `_FRAGMENT_SHADER_TEXTURED` (not solid `PLANKS:*` on post faces). **C4 attachables:** block-model element faces (`orbit_block_model_mesh.py`) — Signature: `orbit-attachable-block-model-faces`; shader stays `tileFrac(worldPos)` only — Signature: `orbit-shader-attribute-blackout`. See `docs/render-types.md` § lessons learned

## Structure tab right column (no gaps when hiding)

The right column uses a flat `QVBoxLayout` (`_structure_tools_layout` in `ui/main_window.py`) — **not** a vertical `QSplitter` between inspector and materials.

When adding or removing a panel from that column:

1. `addWidget(panel)` in stack order (tool hints → `_properties_panel` → `_materials_panel`).
2. Register collapsible panels in `_update_structure_tools_column_layout()` (the loop that sets `QSizePolicy.Maximum` on compass, tool hints, and properties).
3. On every show/hide (close button, View menu, tool toggle): call `_update_structure_tools_column_layout()`.
4. Only **one** stretch target: `_materials_panel` when visible; otherwise a bottom `QSpacerItem` pushes panels to the top.

Do **not** give the whole column `stretch=1` on a splitter or container that stays tall when a child is hidden — that recreates empty gaps below Selected Block / Grid cell.

## Structure tab left column (no gaps when hiding)

The left column uses `_palette_column_layout` in `ui/main_window.py`:

1. **Palettes** — only stretch target (`stretch=1`, grows at the top).
2. **Groups**, **Layers**, **Structure** — `QSizePolicy.Maximum`; call `_update_palette_column_layout()` when hiding Structure (close button or **View → Structure settings**).

Do not put `stretch=1` on the bottom panel or a wrapper that stays tall when Structure is hidden.

## Toolbar vs panel

- **Panel** header icons: 18px, `panel_header` + `make_panel_tool_button`.
- **Grid header** toolbar (eraser/save): 22px, `toolbar_icon_size()`, `LayerActionToolbar` / `QToolBar`.
- **Split toolbar buttons** (Selector, Eraser): see `.cursor/rules/ui-split-buttons.mdc`.

## Panel consistency

When creating a new panel:

- Match existing panel spacing
- Match existing title styling
- Match existing icon sizes
- Match existing visibility behavior
- Reuse existing helpers before creating new UI helpers